    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d390">

                <pb facs="0724" n="686" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv11/pg686"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72119P43/847</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the British Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Grey</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-12-03">December 3, 1919</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your communication dated December 3rd,<anchor n="21a"
                        xml:id="d390-f1"/> in which you state that, according <pb facs="0725"
                        n="687" xml:id="pg687"/> to a message which was received from your
                    Government, it is felt that a good feeling might be created by postponing the
                    departure from Paris of even a part of the American delegation and to inform you
                    that the American delegation has been instructed to leave Paris on December
                    9th.</p>
                <p>The proposal to postpone the departure of the American Commissioners has received
                    the serious consideration of the President and, according to his final decision,
                    they will all leave France on the above mentioned date.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
